  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 129 PM CDT Mon Jul 20 2026\n\nThe center of a strong upper level area of high pressure will move \nfrom over the Rockies today to south of the area by Wednesday. This \nwill suppress any significant weather from forming bringing dry \nweather to western Kansas. There may be a few mid level cumulus \nclouds in the afternoon tomorrow but otherwise expect mostly clear \nskies during this time frame. Towards the surface, light southerly \nwinds are expected through tonight then briefly shift to the \nnortheast tomorrow morning as a weak cold front moves through the \narea. Winds will then shift to the east tomorrow afternoon into \ntomorrow night, then the southeast Wednesday. Very warm conditions \nare expected during this time frame with highs around 100 degrees \nthis afternoon with lows tonight ranging from around 70 degrees along \nthe KS/Co border to upper 70s across south central Kansas. Highs \ntomorrow look to range from the mid 90s along the I-70 corridor to \nlow 100s across south central Kansas. Lows tomorrow night will dip \nto around 70 degrees with the exception of south central Kansas \nwhere low 70s will be found. Highs Wednesday look to reach into the \n90s. \n\nMid range models show a few weak disturbances move over the upper \nlevel ridge Wednesday and Thursday night increasing lift across \nwestern Kansas. As of now, NBM depicts only a slight chance of \nthunderstorms across west central Kansas and the I-70 corridor \nWednesday night with a better chance across the entire CWA Thursday \nnight. A dry and hot pattern then returns for the remainder of the \nforecast. Highs during this time frame will generally be in the 90s \nwith 100s possible along the KS/OK border Thursday and the entire \nCWA Sunday. Lows will generally range from the upper 60s to upper \n70s.",
